patch=1,EE,0013A940,word,0803FAC0
patch=1,EE,0013A944,word,00000000
// Infinite Ammo (Advanced Settings, Off/On, all modes): offline and split-screen only. Sets the game's own infinite-ammo match flag (0x100). Not offered or sent in LAN/online matches, where the game always uses up ammo
// Regeneration / Leech: also set the game's own rank/score display flag (0x8000) in the setup, so the Rank box shows for every player as in the other modes
// Reverse Scoring (Advanced Settings, Capture the Bag, Off/On): normal Capture the Bag, plus you can take your own bag from its base by standing on it for 1 second and score by taking it to an enemy base. Decided by the host, so it works for every player, patched or not
// Score With Bag Away (Advanced Settings, Capture the Bag, Off/On; was "Bag Must Be Home" Yes/No): On lets you score with the enemy bag even while your own bag is away. The host tells every player's game that your bag is home, that you touched your base (so an unpatched game runs a normal capture), then where your bag really is
// Virus: Spread By Kills (Advanced Settings, Virus, Off/On; LAN/online only, decided by the host): the virus spreads only by kills: an infected player's kill infects the victim. Touching no longer infects. Normal Virus scoring
// Team VIP (Advanced Settings, Gladiator, Off/On; the first Gladiator item. Gladiator always shows Team Settings and Spawn Settings, as teams are optional through Team VIP): On makes Gladiator a team mode (team spawns) and the Gladiator is the VIP. Every 5 seconds the VIP's team scores a point and so does every player on it, but only if the VIP has moved at least 10 units since the last tick (no points for camping); killing the VIP gives the killer and their team 3 points and makes the killer the VIP. Decided by the host, so scores reach every player
// Weapon Mode (Advanced Settings: Off / Gun Game / Random Weapon) for Deathmatch, Team Deathmatch, Elimination, Shrink, Vampire, Regeneration, Leech, Gladiator. Gun Game is only offered (and only runs) in Deathmatch, Shrink, Regeneration and Leech with teams off; the other modes, and team games, offer Off / Random Weapon. Decided by the host (or offline game): it hands out weapons from the match's weapon set with the game's own weapon drop (sent to every player, patched or not), carrying the most ammo the game allows; the host sends it to the pad nearest the player (the game's own forced drop pad), so it lands next to them: 2 seconds into the match and half a second after each respawn. Gun Game: no weapon drops when players die, and the map's weapon pickups are collected by the host as soon as every player has loaded (before anyone's 3-2-1 countdown can end, so faster-loading players never see them) and never come back; a player joining mid-match is told again that they were picked up (their game loads the map with every gun showing); everyone climbs the weapon set in order (grenades/mines skipped); kills with your current weapon give you the next one (Kills To Advance, right under Weapon Mode: 1 Kill / 3 / 5 / 10 Kills, default 3; greyed out unless Gun Game is picked, and Player Drops Gun is greyed out while it is; kills with any other weapon do not count); your score is your level; finishing the last weapon wins the match (it ends one frame later, so the game's rankings include the final kill). While Gun Game is chosen (in a mode that can play it): the custom weapon set's weapon picker and slot list grey out the weapons Gun Game cannot hand out (grenades, mines, no-ammo and no-drop weapons), the same way the game greys out the flamethrower in Virus / Flame Tag; Score Limit is greyed out on the match settings page, and the host starts the match with no score limit (sent to every player), so it only ends when someone finishes the ladder or the time runs out. Random Weapon: a random weapon from the set each life; map weapons stay and dropped weapons can be picked up (death drops follow Player Drops Gun). A player joining mid-match starts at level 0 and is given their weapon 2 seconds after the host greets them. Players this game controls (offline, bots, the host's own players) switch to the weapon they are given as soon as they hold it, and the set's other weapons are taken away
// Player Drops Gun (Advanced Settings, every mode: On / Off, default On): Off stops the weapons a player holds from dropping when they die. Decided by the host (or offline game), so it applies to every player
// Always Start With Gun: greyed out in match settings while Gun Game or Random Weapon is picked for a mode that plays it, and the host turns the game's own start-with-gun flag off in its setup, so every player (patched or not) spawns without it
// Spawn Rule (Advanced Settings > Spawn Settings, per mode, every mode but Assault: Default / Away From Enemies / Near Teammates; Near Teammates only in modes that can have teams, Gladiator included). Away From Enemies keeps the quarter of the spawn points furthest from the nearest living enemy; Near Teammates keeps the eighth nearest to a living teammate. In team games the spawn points considered are every player spawn point on the map, not only the team's own base. A player's first spawn of each match (before their first death) always uses the normal team spawn points. In LAN matches the host pre-picks each player's next spawn point when they die; with a rule on, patched consoles instead pick their own player's spawn point at the moment of respawning (live positions), following the host's rule from setup byte 72 (0xB0 | rule). Players without this patch use the host's pre-pick (made with the rule)
// Flame Pass (Advanced Settings, Flame Tag, LAN only: Touch / Kill / Touch Or Kill). Kill: a burning player passes the flame by killing someone not on fire, and touching no longer passes it; Touch Or Kill: both. Decided by the host, which sends who is on fire to every player
// Gold Rush / Coin Drop (Advanced Settings, Thief; Gold Rush was called Gold Rush). Gold Rush (Off/On): nobody drops a coin when they die; instead the host puts a coin on a random spawn point every 5/8 second (the first 3 seconds in; at most 24 on the map, and only while 6 or more of the game's 30 dropped-pickup slots are free, which coins share with dropped guns) and bots without a coin to chase go for it; the spot is one of 48 random navigation pads (the pads players and bots walk on, all over the map; ledge, door, cover, water, teleport and placement pads left out; if none can be used, a spawn point of any arcade mode but Assault) without a coin, picked at random from the quarter of them furthest from the coins already out and from every player and bot, so coins spread over the whole map and don't keep appearing where someone is standing. Each coin disappears after 15 seconds if nobody takes it (it flashes just before; LAN players' copies go half a second earlier, so nobody can take a coin the host no longer has). With Gold Rush, a coin another console says it picked up still scores when this console no longer has it (taken or gone here a moment earlier), so every console counts the same coins. Coin Drop (Any Death / Player Kills; greyed out while Gold Rush is On): Player Kills drops a coin only when another player kills you (no coin for suicides, falls or the level). Decided by the host (or offline game) and sent to LAN players with the Zone Interval byte (setup byte 74, now written at the start of every match, not only in team games); a LAN player without this patch still sees their own dropped coin, but it is not real and scores nothing
// Catch-Up (Advanced Settings, per mode: Off / On, then Catch-Up Period: All Match / Last Minute; greyed out while Catch-Up is Off). Both are greyed out while Weapon Mode is Gun Game (in a mode that can play it), and a Gun Game match never uses Catch-Up. Offered in One On One, Deathmatch, Team Deathmatch, Capture the Bag, Shrink, Thief, Regeneration, Leech, Zones, Gladiator and Monkey Assistant (not Bag Tag, Elimination, Vampire, Flame Tag, Virus or Assault). While it is active, whoever is in last place scores double: in team games the last-placed team. Last place = the lowest ranking score among the ranked players (monkey assistants left out), and only while it is below the leader's, so nobody gets it while everyone is level; tied last places all get it. Every point added to a player's or a team's score counts twice (captures, zone points, coins, Team VIP points), and in the kill-scored modes each kill counts 2 (the extra kills stay for the rest of the match). Last Minute: only while 60 seconds or less of the time limit are left (never without a time limit). Decided by the host (or offline game) and sent to every player with the game's own score updates, so players without the patch see the same scores
// Capture the Bag Overtime (Advanced Settings, Capture the Bag: Off / On). When the time limit runs out while anyone is carrying a bag, the match goes on with a centre-screen "Overtime!" and the game's Text Sweep sound until no bag is being carried (scored, dropped or taken back), then the game's own time-up ends it. Only once per match. Decided by the host (or offline game): it keeps its time limit at 0 during overtime (sent to every player with the game's own score updates) and ends the match itself. LAN players with this patch get the setting in setup byte 72 (bit 2, under the Spawn Rule's 0xB0 marker) and show "Overtime!" too; players without it see "Time Up!" when time runs out but keep playing until the host ends the match
// Random Characters (Advanced Settings, every mode: Off / On). Decided by the host (or offline game): when a match is set up, every player and bot slot gets a random character (any of the 150 in the character list, with its head) before the match starts, so it changes each match. The host's choices go out to everyone with the game's own setup, so players without this patch see the same characters. Not used in Story, Challenge or Arcade League ladder matches; in Monkey Assistant only the players are changed, the monkeys stay monkeys
